# Technologies this project depends on. Kept by security-advisor (dev_team),
# read by cve-watch. Package dependencies come from the lockfiles; list here
# only what they don't cover.
#
# What db_audit_gm runs is ten Docker bricks (bricks/*, images
# 127.0.0.1:5000/dbagm/<brick>:<version>) on debian:13-slim, plus the GM's
# host tool (tools/gmctl, Debian's python3 and python3-yaml). Its one lockfile
# is the api brick's (from v0.5): bricks/api/requirements.txt, 15 hash-pinned
# wheels, read by osv-scanner. Versions below are those in the images built
# from this branch (dpkg-query inside each image, 2026-10-26; postgres 0.4.0,
# bastion 0.4.0 and scheduler 0.2.0 re-checked 2026-10-30; pgbadger in
# postgres 0.4.0 resolved 2026-10-31; pgbouncer 0.1.1 re-checked 2026-11-02,
# same 133 packages as 0.1.0; postgres 0.5.0, scheduler 0.3.0 and api 0.1.0
# resolved 2026-11-03 at v0.5 wave 1's gate G8, bastion 0.5.0 and grafana
# 0.3.0 being the bastion 0.4.0 and grafana 0.2.0 images retagged; pgwatch
# 0.1.0, health-check 0.1.0 and postgres 0.5.0 rebuilt with pgCluu resolved
# 2026-11-04 at v0.5 wave 2's gate G10, grafana 0.3.0 gaining a dashboard
# seed and no package; grafana 0.3.0 rebuilt on Grafana 13.3.0 the same day,
# owner ruling D396, its 129 Debian packages at the versions recorded
# below; bastion 0.5.0 rebuilt with curl at v0.5 wave 4's gate G11.2
# (91aad3f, 157 packages) and prometheus 0.2.0 and postgres-exporter 0.2.0
# read 2026-11-10; grafana 0.3.0 rebuilt on Grafana 13.3.1 (label kept,
# owner ruling D458) and prometheus 0.2.1 on Prometheus 3.16.0 at v0.5
# wave 5's gate G11.4, 2026-11-12, their Debian packages unchanged: 129 and
# 126, prometheus 0.2.1's dpkg-query list identical to 0.2.0's). v0.6 wave 1
# (merge 15a5e1a, gate G5, 2026-11-16): every brick took a new tag, bastion
# 0.6.0, grafana 0.4.0, scheduler 0.4.0, postgres 0.5.1, api 0.1.1,
# health-check 0.1.1, pgbouncer 0.1.2, pgwatch 0.1.1, postgres-exporter 0.2.1,
# prometheus 0.2.2; nine are the v0.5 images retagged (image IDs equal to
# bastion 0.5.0, grafana 0.3.0, postgres 0.5.0, api 0.1.0, health-check 0.1.0,
# pgbouncer 0.1.1, pgwatch 0.1.0, postgres-exporter 0.2.0, prometheus 0.2.1),
# scheduler 0.4.0 is rebuilt with its fill mode (standard library and the
# psycopg it already had, no new package) and its dpkg-query list is identical
# to 0.3.0's (142 packages). No Dockerfile changed a package or a pinned
# download, no lockfile or SBOM changed; dpkg-query read in all ten v0.6
# images 2026-11-16, every version below holds. v0.6 wave 2 (chunk 6, merge
# 153fc24, gate G7, 2026-11-17): bastion 0.6.0 rebuilt with jq and tmux
# (Debian, --no-install-recommends, unpinned), 163 packages: the 157 of 0.5.0,
# six new (jq, libjq1, libonig5, tmux, libevent-core-2.1-7t64, libjemalloc2;
# libutempter0 absent) and PGDG libpq5 and postgresql-client-18 moved from
# 18.6 to 18.7-1.pgdg13+2. v0.6 wave 2's gate G9.1 (2026-11-17, PostgreSQL's
# 2026-11-12 security release): postgres 0.5.1 (c2ebb6cceaed), pgbouncer
# 0.1.2 (387417b98d9e), scheduler 0.4.0 (c368bd08207f), api 0.1.1
# (4518e6873dde) and health-check 0.1.1 (d27fee8b444b) rebuilt --no-cache
# --pull, same tags (unreleased); dpkg-query read in each by the advisor the
# same day and diffed against the previous image: postgres libpq5,
# postgresql-18 and postgresql-client-18 18.6 -> 18.7-1.pgdg13+2;
# pgbouncer the same client pair, libcares2 1.34.5-1+deb13u1 ->
# 1.34.9-1~deb13u1, and PGDG postgresql-client, -client-common, -common and
# -common-dev 293.pgdg13+1 -> 295.pgdg13+1; scheduler and api libpq5 17.11 ->
# 17.12-0+deb13u1; health-check libpq5 and postgresql-client-17 the same;
# nothing else. The G9.1 follow-up (commit 1a123a6, spec D539, 2026-11-18)
# re-pinned postgres 0.5.1's two C extensions to PGDG's rebuilds against
# 18.7 and rebuilt it --no-cache --pull, same tag (unreleased):
# c2ebb6cceaed -> 52300dbef515, dpkg-query read by the advisor and diffed
# (153 packages): postgresql-18-cron 1.6.8-1.pgdg13+2 -> +3 and
# postgresql-18-pgaudit 18.0-3.pgdg13+1 -> +2, nothing else. v0.6 wave 3's
# gate (2026-11-19, 12:21 UTC) rebuilt all ten --no-cache --pull, same tags
# (postgres 91e6d7b6f222, bastion 71e9bbf8733d, pgbouncer a72434f74288,
# health-check 9f6af63b9cf6, ...), dpkg lists unchanged; wave 4's chunk 5
# rebuilt grafana 0.4.0 from cache (46e068499f7e, dashboard JSON only).
# Gate G8 (2026-11-19, 17:00 UTC): dpkg-query read in all ten, every
# version below holds (grafana's 129 packages identical; its grafana and
# plugin binaries equal the SBOMs' hashes). Then apt list --upgradable in
# throwaway containers, and a fresh build's resolution simulated
# (apt-get -s) for the PGDG bricks: two Debian security updates are out
# that the images lack. (1) zlib1g 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+b1 in all ten,
# DSA-6613-1 (2026-11-07) fixes CVE-2026-85091 (gzwrite heap overflow after
# a failed write()) and CVE-2026-27171 (crc32_combine64 CPU, low) at
# +deb13u1. zlib1g comes from the debian:13-slim layer (built 2026-11-04,
# Hub digest a72b4433de1c unchanged on 2026-11-19) and no Dockerfile runs
# apt-get upgrade, so a --no-cache rebuild does NOT pick it up: only a
# refreshed base or a Dockerfile change does (the release gate's G9.3 named it,
# see below: +deb13u1 in all ten since). Not reachable in practice:
# the Go binaries and Python use their own compression, nginx, curl and
# OpenSSH use deflate/inflate, never gzwrite; pg_dump/pg_basebackup's gzip
# output (bastion, postgres) stops at the first failed write. (2) nginx
# DSA-6642-1 (2026-11-19 14:40 UTC), see the nginx entry. PGDG moved on
# 2026-11-17: trixie-pgdg main now carries libpq5 19.0-1.pgdg13+1 (18.x
# libs moved to component 18) and postgresql-18 18.7-1.pgdg13+5 (a rebuild,
# "make space for PostgreSQL 19.0", no security content), postgresql-common
# 297; a fresh build would put libpq5 19.0 in postgres, bastion and
# pgbouncer, and pgbouncer's unpinned postgresql-client metapackage would
# pull postgresql-client-19 (with make and guile through
# postgresql-common-dev 297). None of it is security-motivated (NVD
# PostgreSQL 19.0 and 18.7: 0). A cached
# docker build of a brick keeps its old apt layer: security updates arrive
# only with --no-cache. The Go binaries downloaded
# as release tarballs
# (prometheus, promtool, grafana and its bundled Prometheus data source
# plugin, postgres_exporter, pgwatch) are described by one CycloneDX SBOM
# each, bricks/<brick>/sbom/<binary>.cdx.json, which osv-scanner reads on
# every sweep (the Go toolchain as Go/stdlib, every module go version -m
# reports, the main module where OSV can match its version). tools/go-sbom
# generate <brick> writes them from the exact archive the Dockerfile pins
# (SHA-256 checked; 2026-11-04 each binary's hash equal to the one in the
# built image); tools/tests/test_go_sbom.py fails while an SBOM records
# another version or checksum than its Dockerfile, so a bump must regenerate
# them. Debian package versions carry backported fixes, so an NVD match on
# one is settled by the Debian security tracker.
#
# v0.6 wave 4's G9.2 (owner ruling D587: PostgreSQL 19 everywhere; post-change
# check 2026-11-20). Chunk 17a (merge b788df5) rebuilt six bricks --no-cache on
# PGDG's 19.0, tags kept (master spec 6.8 folds it into the unreleased
# versions): postgres 0.5.1 (a7ba8baf3a3e), bastion 0.6.0 (7f4627becc7a),
# pgbouncer 0.1.2 (9d61f7a8aac7), scheduler 0.4.0 (3c77ec1738a0), api 0.1.1
# (86736f0121cf), health-check 0.1.1 (36d1572dfd7a). Chunk 17b (merge a2dbe23)
# moved postgres-exporter 0.2.1 (f7d469783181) to postgres_exporter 0.21.1 and
# pgwatch 0.1.1 (8ba9681ff1d1) to pgwatch 6.2.0, their Debian packages
# identical to G8's, their SBOMs regenerated. dpkg-query lists diffed against
# G8's by the advisor; nothing else moved: postgres libpq5, postgresql-18 and
# postgresql-client-18 18.7-1.pgdg13+2 -> libpq5, postgresql-19 and
# postgresql-client-19 19.0-1.pgdg13+1, postgresql-18-cron -> postgresql-19-cron
# (1.6.8-1.pgdg13+3 both), postgresql-18-pgaudit 18.0-3.pgdg13+2 ->
# postgresql-19-pgaudit 19.0-1.pgdg13+1; bastion the client pair the same,
# nginx deb13u10 -> deb13u11; pgbouncer the client pair the same, PGDG's
# postgresql-client 18+295 metapackage gone and postgresql-common,
# -client-common and -common-dev PGDG 295.pgdg13+1 -> Debian 278 (with
# libio-pty-perl and libipc-run-perl, 278's -dev dependencies); scheduler and
# api Debian libpq5 17.12-0+deb13u1 -> PGDG 19.0-1.pgdg13+1, ca-certificates
# and openssl added (the PGDG source over HTTPS); health-check the same, and
# Debian postgresql-client-17, postgresql-client 17+278 and
# postgresql-client-common 278 -> PGDG postgresql-client-19 19.0-1.pgdg13+1 and
# postgresql-client-common 297.pgdg13+1, nginx deb13u10 -> deb13u11.
# postgresql-common stays Debian's 278 in postgres, bastion (both since v0.4:
# the first install takes it for PGDG's key, the second does not upgrade it)
# and pgbouncer: kept (advisor, G9.2). PGDG's postgresql-19 Depends
# postgresql-common (>= 275~); OSV Debian:13 postgresql-common 278: 0 (its 3
# CVEs fixed in 178-210); PGDG's 279-297 changelog carries no security fix,
# its 19-specific changes are in pg_upgradecluster and the server build file;
# no brick runs pg_createcluster, pg_ctlcluster or pg_upgradecluster (initdb
# and postgres under s6), only pg_wrapper for the client commands; 297 would
# add systemd-sysusers and -tmpfiles providers. zlib1g stayed
# 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+b1 everywhere at G9.2 (the base layer); D588
# settled it at the release gate, below.
#
# v0.6 release gate, row G9.3 (commit 7476d7b, spec D588; post-change check
# 2026-11-20). Each brick's final-stage install names zlib1g (api's and
# scheduler's in their program stage) and asserts ARG
# ZLIB_FLOOR=1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+deb13u1 with dpkg --compare-versions,
# beside LIBSSL_FLOOR; named rather than apt-get upgrade, which would also move
# postgresql-common 278 to PGDG's 297. All ten rebuilt --no-cache --pull, tags
# kept (unreleased), base still debian@sha256:a72b4433de1c (2026-11-04):
# api 0.1.1 19fed2db7d8d, bastion 0.6.0 f7c1e6e32ec2, grafana 0.4.0
# b0c83ec3fa5c, health-check 0.1.1 9514cf78d394, pgbouncer 0.1.2 83de9e878b02,
# pgwatch 0.1.1 c16b1e4e86f8, postgres 0.5.1 a4f54d67b748, postgres-exporter
# 0.2.1 f23d1f2671d6, prometheus 0.2.2 74152a9ac2cf, scheduler 0.4.0
# 638963de57f5. dpkg-query read in each image by the advisor: identical to the
# builder's lists, zlib1g +b1 -> 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+deb13u1 the only
# difference (143, 163, 129, 152, 134, 126, 153, 129, 126, 144 packages);
# dpkg -V zlib1g clean, libz.so.1.3.1 the same file in all ten; every image's
# history carries the ZLIB_FLOOR assertion; libssl3t64 3.5.7-1~deb13u3 and
# postgresql-common 278 unchanged. OSV Debian:13 zlib +deb13u1: 0 (on +b1: 4,
# CVE-2026-85091, CVE-2026-27171, CVE-2026-76844 and DSA-6613-1 itself).
# DSA-6613-1 fixes CVE-2026-85091 and CVE-2026-27171; CVE-2026-76844 is a
# webpack-dev-middleware path traversal the Debian tracker marks NOT-FOR-US,
# which OSV's Debian import still attaches to zlib (record modified
# 2026-11-14): no zlib issue, and gone on +deb13u1 either way. apt list
# --upgradable in a throwaway container of each image (2026-11-20, after the
# build): nothing from trixie or trixie-security; from PGDG only
# postgresql-common, -client-common, -common-dev 297.pgdg13+1 in postgres,
# bastion and pgbouncer (kept, G9.2) and check-postgres 2.26.0-2.pgdg130+1 in
# health-check (a rebuild, "No source changes"; the image keeps Debian's
# 2.26.0-2). PGDG's 19.0-1.pgdg13+1 still current.
#
# A brick's tag names one Debian package list (owner ruling 2026-11-10): a
# rebuild that changes an image's content (a Debian package version, a pinned
# binary's release) takes the next patch version, with the scenario re-pins in
# the same wave; a rebuild keeps its tag only when its dpkg-query list is
# identical. The per-image versions recorded below rely on it.
schema = 1
updated = 2026-11-20

[stack]
languages = ["Python 3.13", "POSIX shell", "Perl 5.40 (postgres brick: vault-post with core HTTP::Tiny, pgBadger, pgCluu; health-check brick: check_postgres, health-run)"]
frameworks = ["FastAPI 0.162 (api brick)", "Uvicorn 0.54", "Pydantic 2.14", "psycopg 3.3 (api, pure Python over PGDG libpq 19)"]
runtime = ["Docker Engine 29 (swarm mode)", "s6-overlay 3.2", "cron 3.0pl1 (Debian, postgres and health-check bricks)"]
base_image = ["debian:13-slim (Debian 13.7 trixie)"]
data = ["PostgreSQL 19 (PGDG, server, client and libpq in every brick using one; TLS on from postgres 0.5.0, now 0.5.1)", "pg_cron 1.6 (PGDG)", "pgaudit 19.0 (PGDG)", "PgBouncer 1.26 (PGDG)"]
monitoring = ["Prometheus 3.16", "postgres_exporter 0.21", "Grafana 13.3 (bundled Prometheus data source 13.2)", "pgwatch 6.2 (pgwatch brick, Prometheus sink)", "check_postgres 2.26 (Debian, health-check brick)", "pgBadger 13.3 (PGDG, postgres brick)", "pgCluu 5.0 (PGDG, postgres brick)"]
bricks = ["postgres 0.5.1", "bastion 0.6.0", "prometheus 0.2.2", "postgres-exporter 0.2.1", "grafana 0.4.0", "scheduler 0.4.0", "pgbouncer 0.1.2", "api 0.1.1", "pgwatch 0.1.1", "health-check 0.1.1"]
rendering = ["cmark-gfm 0.29 (Debian, bastion starter-pack page)"]
web = ["nginx 1.26 (Debian, bastion web front and health-check status page)"]
clients = ["curl 8.14 (Debian; the bastion players' HTTP client from bastion 0.5.0, now 0.6.0, and in seven other bricks)"]
tools = ["jq 1.7 (Debian; bastion 0.6.0, grafana 0.4.0, postgres-exporter 0.2.1)", "tmux 3.5 (Debian; bastion 0.6.0)"]
bastion_tools = ["psql 19 (PGDG)", "OpenSSH client 10.0", "curl 8.14", "jq 1.7", "tmux 3.5", "openssl 3.5", "less, nano, vim-tiny", "the web front: nginx 1.26 and cmark-gfm 0.29"]
lockfiles = [
    "bricks/api/requirements.txt",  # the api brick's 15 hash-pinned wheels (gate G6); the GM tool uses only Debian's python3-yaml
    # Go modules inside the release binaries, generated by tools/go-sbom (CycloneDX, read as SBOMs)
    "bricks/prometheus/sbom/prometheus.cdx.json",
    "bricks/prometheus/sbom/promtool.cdx.json",
    "bricks/postgres-exporter/sbom/postgres_exporter.cdx.json",
    "bricks/grafana/sbom/grafana.cdx.json",
    "bricks/grafana/sbom/gpx_grafana-prometheus-datasource_linux_amd64.cdx.json",
    "bricks/pgwatch/sbom/pgwatch.cdx.json",
]

# --- the game's host ----------------------------------------------------------

[[platform]]
name = "Docker Engine (armenelos, swarm manager)"
version = "29.9.3"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:docker:engine"
source = "host: docker version on armenelos, 2026-11-16 (client and server 29.9.3, Go 1.26.10, containerd v2.4.2, runc 1.5.2; 29.9.1 on 2026-10-26). NVD (cve-watch latest --version 29.9.3): 0, 2026-11-16"

[[platform]]
name = "Docker Engine (VPS vps-5718ad52, swarm worker from v0.3 wave 3)"
version = "29.9.2"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:docker:engine"
source = "host: ssh vps docker version, 2026-10-26 (client and server 29.9.2, Go 1.26.10, containerd v2.4.2, runc 1.5.2); upgraded by the owner from 28.5.1 the same day"

# --- the shared base of every brick -------------------------------------------

[[platform]]
name = "Debian (base image debian:13-slim)"
version = "13.7"
source = "bricks/*/Dockerfile FROM debian:13-slim (floating tag; 13.7 in the images built 2026-10-26). No cpe: debian:debian_linux matches distribution-wide CVEs, not this image's packages; the packages that matter are listed below"

[[platform]]
name = "s6-overlay"
version = "3.2.3.2"
source = "bricks/*/Dockerfile ARG S6_OVERLAY_VERSION, sha256-pinned release archive. No CPE exists on NVD (checked 2026-10-26); watch github.com/just-containers/s6-overlay"

[[platform]]
name = "OpenSSH server and client"
version = "10.0"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:openbsd:openssh"
source = "Debian openssh-server 1:10.0p1-7+deb13u4 in all ten v0.6 images (apt, unpinned; upstream 10.0p1; dpkg-query 2026-11-16, v0.6 gate G5), on Debian glibc 2.41 (libc6 2.41-12+deb13u4), never musl. sshd: PasswordAuthentication yes on bastion only (the players' login), no elsewhere; UsePAM no everywhere"

[[platform]]
name = "sudo"
version = "1.9.16p2"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:sudo_project:sudo"
source = "Debian sudo 1.9.16p2-3+deb13u2 in the nine v0.6 images other than bastion (apt, unpinned; dpkg-query 2026-11-16, v0.6 gate G5)"

[[platform]]
name = "OpenSSL"
version = "3.5.7"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:openssl:openssl"
source = "Debian libssl3t64 3.5.7-1~deb13u3 (trixie-security) in all ten v0.6 images, the openssl command in bastion 0.6.0, pgbouncer 0.1.2 and postgres 0.5.1 (apt, unpinned; dpkg-query 2026-11-16, v0.6 gate G5). Network-facing in postgres 0.5.1 (server TLS on, the 0.5.0 image); bricks/postgres/Dockerfile asserts the floor ARG LIBSSL_FLOOR=3.5.7-1~deb13u3 (gate G5) and removes ssl-cert's snakeoil pair; bricks/health-check/Dockerfile asserts the same floor (gate G9) for libpq's TLS client (check_postgres and the customer's scripts to PostgreSQL 19 over TLS). pgwatch 0.1.1's collector is a static Go binary on Go's crypto/tls, not OpenSSL; its libssl3t64 serves curl and ssh only. NVD matches 3.5.7 to OpenSSL's 2026-08-25 batch (fix 3.5.8) and 2026-09-29 batch (fix 3.5.9); Debian backported both, DSA-6465-1 (3.5.7-1~deb13u2) and DSA-6531-1 (3.5.7-1~deb13u3), no openssl issue open in trixie on the Debian tracker (2026-11-03): those NVD findings are false positives on these images. Re-checked 2026-11-09 and 2026-11-16 (v0.6): all ten images run 3.5.7-1~deb13u3; the tracker marks every NVD match on 3.5.7 at or above medium (19, CVE-2026-14456 included) fixed in trixie at deb13u2 or deb13u3 (accepted below, owner ruling 2026-11-10). G9.2 (2026-11-20): libssl3t64 unchanged in all ten; scheduler 0.4.0, api 0.1.1 and health-check 0.1.1 now also carry the openssl command (ca-certificates Depends it, added for the PGDG source over HTTPS) and PGDG libpq 19 as their TLS client on it. Open in trixie with no fix (since 2026-11-10; NVD has matched none, so the sweep has not raised them): the Debian tracker lists 10 OpenSSL CVEs vulnerable in trixie, trixie-security and sid alike, no DSA, no no-dsa or postponed tag (OSV Debian:13 openssl 3.5.7-1~deb13u3: 10, no fixed version; rechecked at the release gate, 2026-11-20). Eight are in OpenSSL's advisories of 2026-11-10 and 2026-11-17, all rated Low upstream, fixed in 3.5.10: CVE-2026-95691 (QUIC client, malicious server), -88822 (QUIC, connected socket), -124709 (QUIC server), -95692 and -88823 (AES-GCM-SIV through EVP), -107496 (CMS_encrypt to an attacker's EC certificate), -107493 (PEM_X509_INFO_read with a caller's non-NULL stack; OpenSSL's own callers and TLS CA loading pass NULL), -35190 (TLS 1.3 server with the Suite B cert flag). Two have no OpenSSL advisory yet, only upstream pull requests: -95690 (DTLS out-of-sequence fragments; PR 33729 for 3.5) and -84786 (DANE-enabled TLS client; PR 33634). None is on a path a brick serves: the one OpenSSL TLS server is PostgreSQL 19's, TLS over TCP, no Suite B flag, no DTLS, QUIC, CMS, GCM-SIV or DANE; libpq, OpenSSH and nginx (no TLS listener) use none of them. curl 8.14 in the images speaks HTTP/3 through OpenSSL's own QUIC (nghttp3, no ngtcp2), so CVE-2026-95691 and -88822 are reachable only by a player's own curl --http3 to a hostile server, outside the game's hosts (impact: that curl crashes, or one heap byte). The fix arrives with a trixie DSA (3.5.10's backport), then a --no-cache rebuild and a LIBSSL_FLOOR bump in postgres and health-check. Accepted risk (owner ruling at the release gate's G11, 2026-11-20, \"Release, review later\"): v0.6 ships with the 10 open; no [[ignore]], NVD matching none (the note in the accepted risks below). Review at the first trixie openssl DSA, or 2027-02-01 at the latest"

[[platform]]
name = "curl / libcurl (Debian)"
version = "8.14.1"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:haxx:curl"
source = "Debian curl and libcurl4t64 8.14.1-2+deb13u7 (trixie-security's latest, uploaded 2026-10-14; apt, unpinned), the OpenSSL build (curl -V: libcurl/8.14.1 OpenSSL/3.5.7 with nghttp2, nghttp3, libssh2, librtmp, OpenLDAP, libpsl, libidn2, brotli, zstd). bastion 0.5.0: added with --no-install-recommends (gate G11.2, owner accepted 2026-11-10), the players' HTTP client for the partners' endpoints, run by the unprivileged player, no listener; image built 2026-11-10 from 91aad3f, dpkg-query the same day: 14 packages over bastion 0.4.0, curl, libcurl4t64 and libbrotli1 1.1.0-2+deb13u1, libffi8 3.4.8-2, libgnutls30t64 3.8.9-3+deb13u4, libidn2-0 2.3.8-2, libnghttp2-14 1.64.0-1.1+deb13u1, libnghttp3-9 1.8.0-1, libp11-kit0 0.25.5-3, libpsl5t64 0.21.2-1.1+b1, librtmp1 2.4+20151223.gitfa8646d.1-2+b5, libssh2-1t64 1.11.1-1+deb13u2, libtasn1-6 4.20.0-2+deb13u1, libunistring5 1.3-2 (libldap2 2.6.10+dfsg-1 and libsasl2-2 2.1.28+dfsg1-9 were already there, through libpq5). Also in api 0.1.0, grafana 0.3.0, health-check 0.1.0, pgwatch 0.1.0 and scheduler 0.3.0 (dpkg-query 2026-11-09), prometheus 0.2.0 and postgres-exporter 0.2.0 (dpkg-query 2026-11-10: curl already in their 0.1.0 images), all at deb13u7 with the same libraries as bastion. v0.6 (dpkg-query 2026-11-16, gate G5): curl and libcurl4t64 8.14.1-2+deb13u7 in the same eight, bastion 0.6.0, api 0.1.1, grafana 0.4.0, health-check 0.1.1, pgwatch 0.1.1, scheduler 0.4.0, prometheus 0.2.2 and postgres-exporter 0.2.1; not in pgbouncer or postgres. NVD matches 42 CVEs on 8.14.1 (2026-11-10): 19 fixed by Debian backports up to deb13u7, 1 not affected in Debian (CVE-2026-80231), 22 open in trixie (16 no-DSA minor, 6 unimportant), accepted below until 2027-02-01 or the next trixie curl security upload, whichever comes first. The Debian tracker lists 17 more curl issues open in trixie that NVD has not matched yet (urgency not yet assigned, 2026-11-10; CVE-2026-107928 needs a GnuTLS build, not this one): each surfaces as a new finding once NVD analyses it, triaged then. The pulled-in libraries on the Debian tracker (2026-11-10): brotli, libssh2, libidn2, libpsl, libffi, libtasn1-6, libunistring and nghttp3 nothing open in trixie; gnutls28 6 unimportant (certificate-checking nits; used here only by librtmp); openldap 5 unimportant (slapd, LMDB, NSS); nghttp2 CVE-2026-58055 (the nghttpx proxy, not the library); p11-kit CVE-2026-13757 and -18938 (no-DSA minor, its RPC server, never run; the second 32-bit only); rtmpdump CVE-2026-112060 and -112061 (undetermined: a malicious RTMP server against the client, reached only by a player running curl rtmp:// in their own session); cyrus-sasl2 CVE-2026-107161 (DIGEST-MD5 client plugin overflow, fix due in a trixie point release; that plugin's package libsasl2-modules is in none of the eight images, only libsasl2-modules-db). None gets a platform entry: NVD would add only backport false positives, and their fixes arrive with an unpinned rebuild; they fall under the same acceptance (G11.2). Watch: the Debian tracker's curl, rtmpdump and cyrus-sasl2, and curl.se/docs/vuln-8.14.1.html"

# --- per brick ------------------------------------------------------------------

[[platform]]
name = "PostgreSQL (server and client tools)"
version = "19.0"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:postgresql:postgresql"
source = "PGDG 19.0-1.pgdg13+1 (trixie-pgdg main; PostgreSQL 19 released 2026-11-19; owner ruling D587, v0.6 wave 4's G9.2, chunk 17a merge b788df5; every image below rebuilt --no-cache, dpkg-query 2026-11-19, read by the advisor 2026-11-20). Server: postgres 0.5.1 (a7ba8baf3a3e; postgresql-19, postgresql-client-19, libpq5; TLS on, standby and WAL archiving; ARG PG_MAJOR=19; postgresql-19-jit, only a Recommends, not installed, so no JIT). Clients: bastion 0.6.0 (7f4627becc7a; postgresql-client-19, ARG PG_MAJOR=19), pgbouncer 0.1.2 (9d61f7a8aac7; postgresql-client-19 named, no longer the postgresql-client metapackage), health-check 0.1.1 (36d1572dfd7a; postgresql-client-19 and libpq5 beside Debian check-postgres, PGDG's key copied from a throwaway stage), scheduler 0.4.0 (3c77ec1738a0; libpq5 under Debian python3-psycopg 3.2.6) and api 0.1.1 (86736f0121cf; libpq5 under pure-Python psycopg 3.3.7, never psycopg[binary]); the last three were on Debian's libpq5/psql 17.12-0+deb13u1 (trixie-security) until G9.2, an entry of its own now merged here. Every build asserts libpq5 (and the client and server it installs) at 19.* and no 10-18 package; api and scheduler assert psycopg.pq.version() // 10000 == 19. Only the major is pinned, the minor follows PGDG at build time, so a cached build keeps the old minor; security fixes now come with PGDG's minor releases (next 2027-02-11) and a --no-cache rebuild, no longer with trixie-security's libpq. trixie-pgdg main moves libpq5 to 20 when PostgreSQL 20 ships (late 2027): the 19.* assertions then fail the build, and pinning component 19 or taking 20 is a decision then. 19.0 carries the fixes of the 2026-11-12 batch (in 19 RC2); postgresql.org/support/security lists no advisory affecting 19 (checked 2026-11-20); NVD (cve-watch latest --version 19.0): 0, 2026-11-20. CVE-2026-6460 (C extensions vs ALTER ... SET DATA TYPE): pg_cron and pgaudit are PGDG's builds against 19.0/RC2 (entries below); the contrib modules ship in postgresql-19. Players are the superuser dba and the other roles are the game's own services, so unprivileged-user attacks have no attacker here. Watch: postgresql.org/support/security"

[[platform]]
name = "PgBouncer"
version = "1.26.1"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:pgbouncer:pgbouncer"
source = "bricks/pgbouncer/Dockerfile ARG PGBOUNCER_PACKAGE=1.26.1-1.pgdg13+1 (PGDG, owner ruling D177), unchanged in the G9.1 rebuild (dpkg-query 2026-11-17) and in G9.2's (pgbouncer 0.1.2, 9d61f7a8aac7, dpkg-query 2026-11-19, libcares2 1.34.9-1~deb13u1 too). 1.26.1 (2026-10-14) is upstream's latest and fixes CVE-2026-107348/-107349/-107350; NVD (cve-watch latest --version 1.26.1): 0, 2026-11-17. Watch: pgbouncer.org/changelog.html"

[[platform]]
name = "c-ares (pgbouncer brick)"
version = "1.34.9"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:c-ares:c-ares"
source = "Debian libcares2 1.34.9-1~deb13u1 (trixie-security, DSA-6626-1; apt, unpinned) in pgbouncer 0.1.2, rebuilt --no-cache at v0.6 wave 2's gate G9.1 (image 387417b98d9e, dpkg-query 2026-11-17; 1.34.5-1+deb13u1 before), PgBouncer's resolver for its [databases] hosts through Docker's embedded DNS on the overlay. 1.34.9 (2026-10-20) is upstream's latest; it and DSA-6626-1 close everything open since v0.4: CVE-2025-62408, CVE-2026-33630, -69184, -69186 (DSA-6626-1) and the 11 GHSA advisories of 1.34.9 (tracker TEMP entries, trixie (security) fixed at 1.34.9-1~deb13u1). Checked 2026-11-17: NVD (cve-watch latest --version 1.34.9) 0; OSV Debian:13 c-ares 1.34.9-1~deb13u1 0 (1.34.5-1+deb13u1: 4); the Debian tracker's c-ares lists nothing open in trixie (security). Watch: the Debian tracker's c-ares and github.com/c-ares/c-ares security advisories"

[[platform]]
name = "nginx (bastion web front, health-check status page)"
version = "1.26.3"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:f5:nginx_open_source"
source = "Debian nginx and nginx-common 1.26.3-3+deb13u11 (DSA-6642-1) in bastion 0.6.0 and health-check 0.1.1 since their --no-cache rebuilds of v0.6 wave 4's G9.2 (2026-11-19, dpkg-query read by the advisor 2026-11-20; apt, unpinned; deb13u10 before, from gate G9). health-check serves static files only on :8080 under /health/, reached only through the bastion's web_routes: GET and HEAD, autoindex and server_tokens off, no libnginx-mod-* package and no module loaded, no proxy, fastcgi, uwsgi, scgi, grpc, dav, charset, rewrite, mail or stream directive, no HTTP/2 or 3 (asserted by the Dockerfile on nginx -T), so NVD's module CVEs on 1.26.3 (proxy_v2, grpc, charset, rewrite) have no code path there. The Debian tracker lists only 2 unimportant trixie issues (CVE-2009-4487, CVE-2013-0337; 2026-11-04). G8, 2026-11-19: both images still at deb13u10 (wave 3's --no-cache build came at 12:21 UTC, before the DSA). DSA-6642-1 (2026-11-19 14:40 UTC) fixes 9 CVEs at 1.26.3-3+deb13u11, none reachable in either config: CVE-2026-113425 (mail proxy; mail is a dynamic module, no libnginx-mod-* installed), CVE-2026-118899 (listen ... ssl with TLSv1.3; no TLS listener), CVE-2026-120967 and CVE-2026-123640 (stream ssl_verify_client, ssl_preread; no stream), CVE-2026-121810 (HTTP/3), CVE-2026-123007 and CVE-2026-123633 (HTTP/2; neither config enables http2), CVE-2026-123634 (proxy to a variable server name plus an SSI or mirror subrequest; the bastion proxies its web_routes to set variables but has no ssi or mirror), CVE-2026-125283 (try_files with alias and a map variable built from regex captures; the bastion's only map is $http_upgrade -> $connection_upgrade, no capture, used in neither). NVD has not analysed them yet (cve-watch latest: none listed); OSV Debian:13 nginx deb13u10 lists them, deb13u11 leaves CVE-2026-120993 (stream ssl with proxy_protocol v2; no stream, no fix) and the two unimportant ones. The fix arrives with a --no-cache rebuild of health-check and bastion (bastion's also takes PGDG's libpq5 19.0, see the header). G9.2 (2026-11-20): both images run deb13u11, so the nine are fixed in them; OSV Debian:13 nginx 1.26.3-3+deb13u11 leaves CVE-2026-120993 (stream, none here, no fix) and the two unimportant ones. NVD has still not analysed the nine (cve-watch latest --version 1.26.3, 2026-11-20); once it does they match 1.26.3 here as backport false positives, settled by the Debian tracker. Watch: the Debian tracker's nginx. Release gate (2026-11-20, afternoon): NVD has now analysed DSA-6642-1's CVEs and newly matches older ones on 1.26.3, 14 at or above medium not covered below: eight of DSA-6642-1's nine (CVE-2026-113425, -118899, -121810, -123007, -123633, -123634, -123640, -125283; fix 1.30.7), CVE-2026-15176, -97205 and -97629 (2026-10-14; Debian fixed them at deb13u10) and CVE-2026-42533, -56434 and -60005 (2026-07-15; OSV Debian:13 does not list them on deb13u8 or later). OSV Debian:13 nginx 1.26.3-3+deb13u11: 3 (CVE-2009-4487, CVE-2013-0337, CVE-2026-120993): all 14 are backport false positives on these images, accepted below until 2027-05-01 (owner ruling at G11, 2026-11-20)"

[[platform]]
name = "pg_cron (PostgreSQL extension, postgres brick)"
version = "1.6.8"
source = "bricks/postgres/Dockerfile ARG PG_CRON_PACKAGE=1.6.8-1.pgdg13+3, now PGDG postgresql-19-cron (pinned and asserted by dpkg-query at build; v0.4 gate G5) in postgres 0.5.1 since v0.6 wave 4's G9.2 (image a7ba8baf3a3e, dpkg-query 2026-11-19; on 18 it was postgresql-18-cron 1.6.8-1.pgdg13+3, the G9.1 follow-up's rebuild against 18.7, spec D539). No CPE exists on NVD (checked 2026-10-30), no OSV ecosystem. Upstream 1.6.8 (2026-09-08) is the latest release, no repository advisory (2026-11-19, G9.2 preflight). Of PGDG's three postgresql-19-cron builds only +3 Depends postgresql-19 (>> 19~rc2), built against the RC2 that carries the 2026-11-12 fixes; +1 and +2 Depend postgresql-19 unversioned. So +3 closes the extension half of CVE-2026-6460 on 19 as the 18 rebuild did on 18.7 (never reachable as an attack here: only the superuser dba and the game's own service roles connect; pg_cron reads its own cron.job table) (advisor, G9.2). A later PGDG rebuild against a newer minor is a re-pin, not an apt upgrade: the build asserts the exact version. Watch: github.com/citusdata/pg_cron and the Debian tracker's pg-cron"

[[platform]]
name = "cron (Debian, postgres and health-check bricks)"
version = "3.0pl1-197"
source = "Debian cron and cron-daemon-common 3.0pl1-197 in postgres 0.5.1 (apt, unpinned; gate G5) and health-check 0.1.1 (gate G9: postgres's spool crontab only, /etc/crontab and the cron.d and run-parts entries removed; re-checked 2026-11-04). Debian's own Vixie cron fork, versioned by its Debian revision: no CPE fits (none for vixie cron on NVD, checked 2026-10-30; NVD's 3.0 hits such as CVE-2019-9706 are fixed in 3.0pl1-133). The Debian tracker's source package cron is the watch (no open issue in trixie as of 2026-10-30; OSV Debian:13 cron 3.0pl1-197 clean 2026-11-04)"

[[platform]]
name = "pgBadger (PostgreSQL log analyser, postgres brick)"
version = "13.3"
source = "PGDG pgbadger 13.3-1.pgdg13+1 in postgres 0.5.1 (bricks/postgres/Dockerfile, apt, unpinned, installed with postgresql-${PG_MAJOR}; build asserts pgbadger --version), in the image since 0.3.0 (13.2 until 0.4.0); Perl script on Debian perl 5.40.1-6+deb13u1, which also runs vault-post (core HTTP::Tiny 0.088) from 0.5.0. Players run it by hand on the file log, writing HTML reports in their home (brick.yaml report_tools); no daemon, no listener. No CPE exists on NVD and NVD has no CVE mentioning pgbadger (checked 2026-10-31); no OSV record (Debian:13 query clean), no GitHub advisory and no SECURITY.md on github.com/darold/pgbadger, no issue on the Debian tracker's source package pgbadger. 13.3 (2026-11-03) is upstream's latest release, a maintenance release with no security note (it sanitises database names used as paths with --explode; checked 2026-11-03). Watch: darold/pgbadger releases and the Debian tracker"

[[platform]]
name = "pgCluu (PostgreSQL performance reports, postgres brick)"
version = "5.0"
source = "bricks/postgres/Dockerfile ARG PG_CLUU_PACKAGE=5.0-1.pgdg13+1 (PGDG pgcluu, pinned and asserted by dpkg-query at build; gate G9) in postgres 0.5.1 (in the image since 0.5.0's 2026-11-04 rebuild), not Debian's 4.0-1 (no PostgreSQL 17/18 collection). Perl scripts run by hand by the player (pgcluu_collectd --disable-sar --disable-pidstat, then pgcluu -o in their home), never a daemon, no sudo rule; its report CGI /usr/lib/cgi-bin/pgcluu.cgi and /etc/apache2/conf-available/pgcluu.conf deleted and asserted gone, no web server, no sysstat. Brings Debian libjs-jquery 3.6.1+dfsg+~3.5.14-1 and libjs-underscore 1.13.4~dfsg+~1.11.4-3 for the HTML report: underscore 1.13.4 is affected by CVE-2026-27601 (GHSA-qpx9-hpmf-5gmw, unbounded recursion in _.flatten and _.isEqual, fix 1.13.8; open in trixie), a denial of service in the browser of whoever opens a report built from their own collection: not reachable as an attack. No CPE exists on NVD (checked 2026-11-04); OSV Debian:13 pgcluu clean, no GitHub advisory on github.com/darold/pgcluu. Watch: darold/pgcluu releases, the Debian tracker's pgcluu and underscore"

[[platform]]
name = "check_postgres (health-check brick)"
version = "2.26.0"
source = "bricks/health-check/Dockerfile ARG CHECK_POSTGRES_PACKAGE=2.26.0-2 (Debian check-postgres, no recommends, pinned and asserted by dpkg-query and --version at build; gate G9) in health-check 0.1.1. Perl script on Debian perl 5.40.1-6+deb13u1 over PGDG psql/libpq 19.0 (postgresql-client-19 named beside it from v0.6 wave 4's G9.2, Debian's psql 17 before; the build asserts psql --version 19; the PostgreSQL entry), run as postgres from its spool crontab every five minutes (--timeout=15, each run bounded at 30 s) against the scenario's PostgreSQL 19 nodes over TLS, the password in PGPASSFILE, never --dbpass. No CPE exists on NVD (checked 2026-11-04); OSV Debian:13 check-postgres clean, no issue on the Debian tracker. Upstream (github.com/bucardo/check_postgres) dormant since its 2.26.0 release in 2023: a future fix may come only as a Debian patch. Watch: the Debian tracker's check-postgres and perl"

[[platform]]
name = "pgaudit (PostgreSQL extension, postgres brick)"
version = "19.0"
source = "bricks/postgres/Dockerfile ARG PG_AUDIT_PACKAGE=19.0-1.pgdg13+1 (PGDG postgresql-19-pgaudit, pinned and asserted by dpkg-query and pgaudit.so at build; v0.5 gate G5) in postgres 0.5.1 since v0.6 wave 4's G9.2 (image a7ba8baf3a3e, dpkg-query 2026-11-19; postgresql-18-pgaudit 18.0-3.pgdg13+2 on 18 before, spec D539). The release build, Depends postgresql-19 (>> 19.0); PGDG's 19~rc1 builds are never used. Writes DDL, WRITE and ROLE lines to the file log the players read and redacts passwords in role statements itself (password <REDACTED>); PostgreSQL's own statement logging does not, so the password sessions run with pgaudit.log and statement logging off. 19.0 logs differently from 18.0 (only a statement's own permission check, no inserted/updated columns against the SELECT grant, COPY row counts; the changes 18.1 brought on 18): the faults reading audit lines are re-checked on 19 by chunk 17c, a game-content matter, not a security one. No CPE exists on NVD (checked 2026-11-03), no OSV ecosystem (CVE-2025-23413 is F5's, not pgaudit's), no repository advisory (2026-11-19, G9.2 preflight). Watch: github.com/pgaudit/pgaudit security advisories and releases, PGDG pgaudit-19"

[[platform]]
name = "cmark-gfm (bastion starter-pack page)"
version = "0.29.0.gfm.13"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:github:cmark-gfm"
source = "Debian cmark-gfm, libcmark-gfm0.29.0.gfm.13 and libcmark-gfm-extensions0.29.0.gfm.13 0.29.0.gfm.13-4 in bastion 0.6.0 (apt, unpinned; gate G13), run at start-up as cmark-gfm -e table in safe mode (never --unsafe) on the GM's starter-pack files. Watch: upstream silent since 2023 (last release 0.29.0.gfm.13, July 2023); github/cmark-gfm took two commits since (2025-12 a cmake bump, 2026-09 PR #394 an undefined-behaviour fix in the autolink extension, no advisory, not enabled here) but no release, so a future fix may come only as a Debian patch"

[[platform]]
name = "jq (Debian; bastion, grafana, postgres-exporter)"
version = "1.7.1"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:jqlang:jq"
source = "Debian jq and libjq1 1.7.1-6+deb13u4 (trixie-security's latest) with libonig5 6.9.9-1+b1 (apt, unpinned): bastion 0.6.0 (bricks/bastion/Dockerfile, --no-install-recommends, chunk 6 at 153fc24, gate G6 cleared 2026-11-17; master spec 7.7: the players read Prometheus' API and the partners' status file with it, run as the unprivileged player on JSON from the game's own services), grafana 0.4.0 and postgres-exporter 0.2.1 (in their Dockerfiles before v0.6, never recorded until G7; the same versions); dpkg-query in all three images 2026-11-17 (G7). jq --version reports jq-1.7. NVD matches 17 CVEs on 1.7.1 (2026-11-17), every one fixed in trixie at or below deb13u4 on the Debian tracker (1.7.1-6 to 1.7.1-6+deb13u3): backport false positives, accepted below (owner, 2026-11-17). The tracker also lists CVE-2026-39956 and CVE-2026-40164, fixed in deb13u2, that NVD has not matched yet; they would fall under the same reasoning when it does. Open in trixie: only CVE-2025-9403 (DEBIAN-CVE-2025-9403 on OSV, Debian unimportant: the test suite, jq --run-tests, never run here). Oniguruma (libonig5) clean on OSV Debian:13 and the tracker. Watch: the Debian tracker's jq and libonig"

[[platform]]
name = "tmux (Debian; bastion)"
version = "3.5a"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:tmux_project:tmux"
source = "Debian tmux 3.5a-3 with libevent-core-2.1-7t64 2.1.13-stable-1~deb13u1 and libjemalloc2 5.3.0-3 in bastion 0.6.0 (bricks/bastion/Dockerfile, --no-install-recommends, unpinned; libutempter0, a Recommends, absent, so no utmp entries; chunk 6 at 153fc24, gate G6 cleared 2026-11-17; dpkg-query 2026-11-17, G7). Run by the player in their own SSH session (master spec 7.7), no setuid, no listener beyond its per-user socket under /tmp. NVD (cve-watch latest --version 3.5a): 0, 2026-11-17; CVE-2026-11623 is 3.6a's (Debian tracker: trixie not affected, unimportant). OSV Debian:13 tmux, libevent and jemalloc clean, nothing open in trixie on the tracker (2026-11-17). Watch: the Debian tracker's tmux and libevent"

[[platform]]
name = "Prometheus"
version = "3.16.0"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:prometheus:prometheus"
source = "bricks/prometheus/Dockerfile ARG PROMETHEUS_VERSION=3.16.0, sha256-pinned release tarball (68727009472a2c02e1ff7f062fd5b3e637285bffc8fc2d340c76fb449d6e0f34) in prometheus 0.2.2 (v0.6; the 0.2.1 image of v0.5 wave 5, spec D445/D446/D448, gate G11.4; 3.13.5 on the 3.13 LTS line until 0.2.0: from 0.2.1 the brick follows minor releases, D446). From v0.5 a scenario's scrape configuration may add a pgwatch job (<node>:9188, the overlay only). Built image 2026-11-12: prometheus and promtool --version 3.16.0 (revision e2e28ade), binary SHA-256 fe1fc9a01dbe... and a3c953f444da... equal to the SBOMs'. NVD (cve-watch latest --version 3.16.0: 0) and OSV Go module github.com/prometheus/prometheus v0.316.0 (0) clean, 2026-11-12. Embedded modules: bricks/prometheus/sbom/prometheus.cdx.json (242 components) and promtool.cdx.json (199), go1.27.3, the main module as its Go tag v0.316.0 (the binary's own build info would match every advisory). Fixed by 3.16.0: GHSA-2v4p-qf9q-27wj (grpc 1.84.0) and GO-2026-6865 (klauspost/compress 1.20.3). Left, none reachable (go tool nm on the built image's unstripped binaries, 2026-11-12): GO-2026-6860/6866 (x/net 0.61.0, no x/net/html symbol linked), GO-2026-5932 (x/crypto/openpgp, no symbol) and GO-2022-0635/0646 (aws-sdk-go S3 crypto, no s3crypto symbol, no fix exists); GO-2026-6859 (stdlib < 1.27.4, net/http MaxBytesReader race) is open in SECURITY_TODO.md, untriaged"

[[platform]]
name = "postgres_exporter"
version = "0.21.1"
source = "bricks/postgres-exporter/Dockerfile ARG PG_EXPORTER_VERSION=0.21.1 (0.20.1 until v0.6 wave 4's G9.2, chunk 17b, merge a2dbe23), the release tarball, ADD --checksum=sha256:02f316da4e9e409749d6f3b25102d3561cb408023110f3653f6514548926ff0c (equal to upstream's sha256sums.txt), in postgres-exporter 0.2.1 (image f7d469783181, built 2026-11-19, its Debian packages identical to G8's). No CPE exists on NVD (checked 2026-10-26); OSV Go module github.com/prometheus-community/postgres_exporter 0.21.1: 0 (2026-11-20). Embedded modules: bricks/postgres-exporter/sbom/postgres_exporter.cdx.json, regenerated by tools/go-sbom (34 components; binary SHA-256 cb30bff3241e..., equal to the release archive's): go1.27.4, lib/pq 1.12.3, x/net 0.62.0, x/crypto 0.58.0, x/text 0.43.0. The 34 SECURITY_TODO.md findings of 0.20.1's go1.26.4, x/net 0.55.0, x/crypto 0.53.0 and x/text 0.38.0 (none reachable as run) and GO-2026-6809 are gone (cve-watch check 2026-11-20; OSV stdlib 1.27.4: 0). Left: GO-2026-5932 (x/crypto/openpgp, a module-level record): no openpgp package is linked (go tool nm on the release binary, 2026-11-20: x/crypto's bcrypt, blowfish, chacha20, chacha20poly1305, cryptobyte and internal only). Runs plain HTTP/1 on 9187 (handlers /metrics and /), lib/pq on sslmode=disable; the address and password file passed as --datasource.uri and --datasource.pass-file (0.21 deprecates DATA_SOURCE_URI and DATA_SOURCE_PASS_FILE), the user still as DATA_SOURCE_USER. Watch: github.com/prometheus-community/postgres_exporter releases"

[[platform]]
name = "pgwatch (pgwatch brick)"
version = "6.2.0"
source = "bricks/pgwatch/Dockerfile ARG PGWATCH_VERSION=6.2.0 (6.1.0 until v0.6 wave 4's G9.2, chunk 17b, merge a2dbe23), the release tarball pgwatch_Linux_x86_64.tar.gz, ADD --checksum=sha256:8c61a80eb7a68023896029c339b83c1938c557e94ce9aba6140e86b3788c1e51 (equal to upstream's checksums.txt; not the .deb), in pgwatch 0.1.1 (image 8ba9681ff1d1, built 2026-11-19, its Debian packages identical to G8's). Only the binary is installed, /usr/local/bin/pgwatch (go1.26.11, static), with its built-in metric definitions; the build asserts the banner Version: 6.2.0 and that the basic preset needs no init SQL (instance_up, db_size, db_stats and wal need no 19-specific SQL). Run as pgwatch 990 with --web-disable=all (nothing on :8080), a Prometheus sink on :9188 (the overlay only), the basic preset, the password in PGPASSFILE; never --create-helpers or --try-create-listed-exts-if-missing. No CPE exists on NVD (checked 2026-11-04); OSV Go module github.com/cybertec-postgresql/pgwatch/v6 6.2.0, pgx/v5 5.12.0 and stdlib 1.26.11: 0 (2026-11-20). Embedded modules: bricks/pgwatch/sbom/pgwatch.cdx.json, regenerated by tools/go-sbom (46 components, binary SHA-256 53a9db8e1d30..., x/net 0.62.0), read by the daily sweep: no finding (cve-watch check 2026-11-20); 6.1.0's GO-2026-6809 (stdlib x509 distrust list), GO-2026-6859 (stdlib) and GO-2026-6860/6866 (x/net/html), none reachable then, are gone. Watch: github.com/cybertec-postgresql/pgwatch releases and security advisories"

[[platform]]
name = "Grafana"
version = "13.3.1"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:grafana:grafana"
source = "bricks/grafana/Dockerfile ARG GRAFANA_VERSION=13.3.1, GRAFANA_BUILD=42849527790, sha256-pinned release tarball (6acf8939dd2f73332cbcafc27a33973fb1115b8867e7ffa3223c6e2ecbed8531; v0.5 wave 5, spec D445/D446/D448, gate G11.3; was 13.3.0, owner ruling D396, and 13.2.4 before; the brick label stayed 0.3.0, owner ruling D458; v0.6 tags that image grafana 0.4.0). grafana 0.3.0 adds an optional pgwatch dashboard seed (JSON over the Prometheus series, no plugin). Built image 2026-11-12: grafana --version 13.3.1, binary SHA-256 f62d1816778c... and the bundled plugin's f1458b7bacfe... equal to the SBOMs'. The players log in as Grafana's administrator (the tools password). Fixed by 13.3.1 (its release notes; NVD published them 2026-11-11 with no CPE configuration yet, so cve-watch latest does not list them): CVE-2026-102589 (image-renderer key accepted across instances sharing renderer_token; no renderer here), CVE-2026-107509 (a Viewer crashes Grafana with an SQL Expression cast; the players are its administrators already), CVE-2026-110992, CVE-2026-111024, CVE-2026-13721 and CVE-2026-14242 (Git Sync provisioning path traversal and folder-permission bypasses; no Git Sync repository): none reachable as an attack here. Not in 13.3.1's notes: CVE-2026-110289 (GHSA-97fx-j86f-w2rp, Git Sync connection SSRF by an Org Admin, published 2026-11-11 with no affected or fixed range anywhere; no Git Sync connection here and the Org Admin is the players' own account): watch for its range. The grafana.com 2026-10-27 batch (CVE-2026-100105, -88858, -88967; CVE-2026-103506 behind the kubernetesSsoSettingsApi toggle, not set) fixed since 13.3.0. NVD (cve-watch latest --version 13.3.1: 0) and OSV clean 2026-11-12. Embedded modules: bricks/grafana/sbom/grafana.cdx.json (520 components, go1.27.3; main module left out: built as (devel), and OSV's Go records for github.com/grafana/grafana have no fixed version, so NVD above is its check; x/net 0.62.0, GO-2026-6860/6866 gone) and gpx_grafana-prometheus-datasource_linux_amd64.cdx.json (the kept bundled Prometheus data source plugin, plugin.json 13.2.5, its backend go1.27.3, stripped, 104 components; a child process on loopback gRPC with go-plugin's mTLS, an HTTP/1 client to Prometheus; brotli 1.2.7, so GO-2026-6888 is fixed, which was reachable through a data source a player points at their own server). Left, none reachable (2026-11-12): in grafana, GO-2026-5932 (x/crypto/openpgp) and GO-2022-0635/0646 (aws-sdk-go S3 crypto, no fix exists), modules only, no openpgp or s3crypto symbol (go tool nm); in the plugin, GO-2026-6860/6866 (x/net 0.61.0), no x/net/html function in its pclntab; in both, GO-2026-6859 (stdlib < 1.27.4), open in SECURITY_TODO.md, untriaged. The grafana.com catalogue's plugin 13.2.6 exists, not pinned (no security reason, G11.3)"

[[platform]]
name = "Python"
version = "3.13.5"
cpe = "cpe:2.3:a:python:python"
source = "Debian python3.13 3.13.5-2+deb13u5 (apt, unpinned; dpkg-query 2026-11-16): scheduler 0.4.0 (with python3-psycopg 3.2.6-1, python3-yaml 6.0.2; its fill mode adds no import beyond the standard library and psycopg), api 0.1.1 (with python3-yaml 6.0.2 and libyaml-0-2 0.2.5-2, safe loading only, gate G11.1; its PyPI wheels in bricks/api/requirements.txt, no pip in the image) and the GM host's python3 running tools/gmctl (armenelos upgraded from 3.13.5-2+deb13u4 to deb13u5 on 2026-11-10 after its stale trixie main Packages list was removed; apt-cache policy python3.13: installed 3.13.5-2+deb13u5, candidate the same; dpkg-query on the host 2026-11-16: python3.13 3.13.5-2+deb13u5, python3-yaml 6.0.2-1+b2; tools/gm/fill.py imports only the standard library, PyYAML and tools/gm itself)"

